.0,0.0,-2.4914430468925275e-05,0.0,0.0,-0.0006561510381288826,-3.6954811548639555e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,4340,1657,8153,10747,374,894,6716,315,15279,11067,315,264,5792,12371,6113,448,3108,315,220,21,8153,30,17399,697,4226,304,44548,17855,1352,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nHow many units apart is any pair of parallel sides of a regular hexagon with side of 6 units? Express your answer in simplest radical form.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"b0c864f27287856360fda3e11656a529cc49721449efde5d17ce3ded82e3d3d5"},"seconds":20.56067681312561,"seed":619239545251253694,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we'll follow a step-by-step approach:\n\n1. **Understand the Geometry of a Regular Hexagon:**\n   A regular hexagon can be divided into 6 equilateral triangles. Each side of the hexagon is a side of one of these equilateral triangles.\n\n2. **Identify the Distance Between Parallel Sides:**\n   In a regular hexagon, the distance between any pair of parallel sides corresponds to the height of two of these equilateral triangles stacked on top of each other.\n\n3. **Calculate the Height of an Equilateral Triangle:**\n   Let's denote the side length of the equilateral triangle by \\( s = 6 \\) units.\n   The height \\( h \\) of an equilateral triangle can be calculated using the formula for the height of an equilateral triangle:\n   \\[\n   h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} s\n   \\]\n   Substituting \\( s = 6 \\):\n   \\[\n   h = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 6 = 3\\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the Distance Between Parallel Sides:**\n   Since the distance between any pair of parallel sides of the hexagon is twice the height of one equilateral triangle:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance} = 2 \\times 3\\sqrt{3} = 6\\sqrt{3}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Final Answer:**\n   The distance between any pair of parallel sides of the hexagon is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{6\\sqrt{3}}\n   \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{6\\sqrt{3}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
